  "critical_issue": "Discrepancy where 1h-6h-CLOSE_TO_CLOSE had point estimate 1.593 falling outside reported CI [0.775, 1.450].",
  "root_cause_analysis": {
    "root_cause": "Estimand and transformation mismatch between reported point estimate and confidence interval.",
    "mathematical_explanation": "In previous code, t_mean_r was computed as the arithmetic mean of event ratios (1/N * sum(r_i) = 1.593). However, the confidence interval was constructed in log-space: t_ci_log = t_log_mean +- 1.96*SE, and exponentiated: (exp(lower), exp(upper)) = [0.775, 1.450]. The exponent of the mean of log-ratios is the geometric mean (1.060), NOT the arithmetic mean! By the AM-GM inequality, Arithmetic Mean >= Geometric Mean, with strictly greater disparity under skewed volatility ratios. The point estimate was reporting Arithmetic Mean while the CI belonged to Geometric Mean.",
    "remediation_implemented": "Aligned the primary reported point estimate (train_mean_ratio / holdout_mean_ratio) to the exact estimand targeted by the log-scale confidence interval: the geometric mean ratio exp((1/N)*sum(ln(r_i))). Arithmetic means are also preserved and disclosed in distinct fields (train_arithmetic_mean_ratio, holdout_arithmetic_mean_ratio). This guarantees CI_lower <= point_estimate <= CI_upper across 100% of cells."
  },
